revision.text:
{{YFHR|126}}

==Events==
* Wild mage [[Quake Lavender]] recruits her mentor [[Hornung]] the Anarch into the [[Xaositects]].<ref name="fm156">{{b|Planescape|The Factol's Manifesto|pdf=17275|page=156}}</ref>
* [[Pelimo]], owner of [[Fineweave Rugs and Carpets]], disappears after receiving a shipment of rugs imported from across the planes. He is presumed dead, and leaves behind a widow [[Ajami]] and their seven children.<ref name="pokaic13">{{b|Planescape|Planes of Conflict|pdf=17278|page=13, Adventures in Conflict}}</ref>
* A [[githzerai]] discovers his master, [[Bilfar]], dead. The killers reveal themselves: a group of [[cranium rat]]s, agents of the [[Us]]. They offer to the githzerai to join them. He agrees, calling himself [[Parakk]] the Ratcatcher, a word that means both servant and master in the githzerai tongue.<ref name="uncaged7677">{{b|Planescape|Uncaged: Faces of Sigil|pdf=17285|page=76-77}}</ref>


== Background Information ==
* Given in-universe time seems to advance at the same rate as the real world, these products released in 1994 are assumed to be set during this period:
** {{b|Planescape|Planescape Campaign Setting|pdf=17267}}
** {{b|Planescape|The Eternal Boundary|pdf=17300}}
** {{b|Planescape|Planescape Monstrous Compendium Appendix}}
** {{b|Planescape|Planes of Chaos|pdf=17298}}
** {{b|Planescape|Well of Worlds|pdf=17269}}
** {{b|Planescape|In the Abyss|pdf=17270}}
** {{b|Planescape|The Deva Spark|pdf=17271}}



