{{YFHR|130}}

==Events==
* [[Ronassic]] of Sigil publishes a treatise on the ethereal sea, ''[[A Guide to the Ethereal Plane]]''.<ref name="gttep4">{{b|Planescape|A Guide to the Ethereal Plane|pdf=17293|nip=1|page=4}}</ref><ref name="dvd131">{{b|D&D|Die Vecna Die!|pdf=17483|nip=1|page=131}}</ref>
* Factol [[Lhar]] succumbs to the [[Grim Retreat]], and places [[Sruce]] in charge.<ref name="fw38">{{b|Planescape|Faction War (book)|alt=Faction War|pdf=17299|page=38}}</ref>
* The [[Faction War]]. [[Factol]] [[Rowan Darkwood]] enacts an elaborate plan to take over [[Sigil]], deposing the [[Lady of Pain]]. The plan involves all-out war between the various [[faction]]s. Darkwood's plan ultimately fails, but the Lady pronounces: ''This city tolerates your faction no longer. Abandon it or die.'' Unsure if by "it" she means "your faction" or "the city," various factions either splinter, merge, or leave Sigil entirely.<ref name="fw114">{{b|Planescape|Faction War (book)|alt=Faction War|pdf=17299|page=114}}</ref>

== Background Information ==
* Given in-universe time seems to advance at the same rate as the real world, these products released in 1998 are assumed to be set during this period:
** {{b|Planescape|Planescape Monstrous Compendium Appendix III|pdf=17294}}
** {{b|Planescape|Tales from the Infinite Staircase|pdf=17291|nip=1}}
** {{b|Planescape|A Guide to the Ethereal Plane|pdf=17293|nip=1}}
** {{b|Planescape|Faction War (book)|alt=Faction War|pdf=17299}}
** {{b|Planescape|The Inner Planes|pdf=17296|nip=1}}

